The files under src/, README.md, consumer-rules.pro, and proguard-rules.pro were
copied from that checkout; the small source changes listed below are the only local
runtime deviations. The Gradle build file was adapted to the
My-System-App convention plugins and dependency catalog so the source is
compiled by this repository's Kotlin and Compose toolchain. First-party
ktlint/Detekt tasks are disabled for this third-party module so upstream source
can remain byte-for-byte identical; compile and upstream unit tests remain
enabled.

Local source compatibility changes, if required, are recorded below:
  - Added FocusItemView.requestRotaryFocus() and routed controller/area initial-focus requests
    through it. Android rejects requestFocus() for non-touch-focusable views while a window is in
    touch mode; the temporary flag is restored immediately. This lets an app launched by intent
    receive its first rotary focus without requiring an extra detent, while preserving the
    upstream focus policy for subsequent navigation.
  - Deferred FocusArea geometry validation by 120 ms on the main looper so Compose AndroidView
    replacement can detach the outgoing area before validation. Persistent overlap is still
    reported or failed according to RotaryValidationMode; this only removes a one-frame hand-off
    false positive.

